'''Mas Vell''' is a municipality in the [[Cumará (comarca)|Cumará comarca]], [[Estret Province]], [[Balboa]]. With a population of 101,382 in 2026, it is a lower-density suburban municipality situated between the coastal communities of western Cumará and the inland commuter corridor. The municipality is characterised by a quieter residential pattern, with detached housing and low-rise apartment buildings set among landscaped grounds and tree-lined streets, contrasting with the denser development of neighbouring [[Enllaç]] and [[La Cruïlla]].

== Geography ==

Mas Vell occupies a gently sloping position in the western interior of Cumará, between the coastal strip and the foothills of the [[Yalabirga Mountain Range|Yalabirga]] range. The terrain rises from approximately 50 metres in the west to 150 metres in the east. Several small streams cross the municipality, draining westward toward the coast. The landscape is a mix of residential development, landscaped green space, and remnant agricultural land.

=== Climate ===

Mas Vell has a {{w|tropical monsoon climate}} ({{w|Köppen climate classification|Köppen}} Am), with average daily highs of 30 to 32 °C and lows of 22 to 24 °C. Annual precipitation averages approximately 2,200 to 2,500 mm, with the wet season from May to November.

== Demographics ==

Mas Vell's population of 101,382 is composed predominantly of [[Black Balboan people|Black Balboans]] and mixed Balboans, with a small but growing [[Fosian Balboan|Fosian]] community. The municipality's quieter residential character attracts families and older residents, and the average household size is slightly smaller than the comarca average.

== Economy ==

The economy of Mas Vell is based primarily on residential services and local retail. The municipality functions as a commuter suburb, with a significant proportion of residents commuting to [[Sant Cristòfor]], [[Enllaç]], or the [[International City of Areza]] for employment. Local commercial activity is concentrated along the main road corridors, with neighbourhood retail, restaurants, and small service businesses. The municipality has no significant industrial base.

== Transport ==

Mas Vell is connected to the surrounding municipalities by local roads and bus routes. The municipality does not have a CristoCarril rail station; the nearest rail access is at [[Enllaç]] or [[La Cruïlla]] on the main commuter corridor. Bus routes operated by the Varakí municipal transport authority connect Mas Vell to [[Varakí]] and the surrounding Cumará communities.

